2026-11-04 15:13:13.0023 - DEBUG - graphrag.api.index - {'entities': [{'id': 'cbc02f76-b3f9-45ac-ae5b-14d98d061239', 'human_readable_id': 0, 'title': 'PROJECT GUTENBERG', 'type': 'ORGANIZATION', 'description': "Project Gutenberg is a pioneering initiative dedicated to the creation and distribution of free electronic books, often referred to as eBooks. This undertaking relies heavily on the committed efforts of both volunteers and employees who engage in activities such as identifying, researching, transcribing, and proofreading works that are in the public domain. Originally conceptualized by Professor Michael S. Hart, Project Gutenberg operates as a volunteer-driven organization that has made significant contributions to the accessibility of literary works for the public.\n\nProject Gutenberg is responsible for assembling a vast collection of free electronic works with a primary mission of promoting the free distribution of such works. This has allowed them to amass an extensive archive of literary materials, many of which are public domain texts within the United States. A notable aspect of Project Gutenberg's offerings includes significant titles such as 'How to Invest Money,' which the organization has made available for free distribution as a public domain work.\n\nThe initiative is sustained through public donations and the tireless work of its volunteers. These volunteers contribute by ensuring that the texts are properly transcribed and proofread, ensuring high quality for readers while maintaining the works as true to their original form as possible. Users of Project Gutenberg must agree to a specific license when downloading materials, which underscores the organization's commitment to legally distributing these texts in a manner that respects copyright laws while honoring the intentions of public domain initiatives.\n\nOverall, Project Gutenberg represents a remarkable achievement in the pursuit of educational and literary accessibility, continually expanding its offerings and facilitating public access to digitized versions of a wide array of historical texts and literary treasures.", 'text_unit_ids': ['69b0e67c5fa9a5c565b1ea749505fd17c5c4af6ffd0316151c996811d2e0af417ae08600bea4659287b6631162541117c43dfe4a8e29abf6a9ff98e394a00e33', '4d53b154bd12c2d67fa71e4903629fce3f712b84bef668891feedc8e67e5dfed7165bd5f38fa34cca09426adfd5441fa45f95f26684e1bbd0666493af5dd0868', 'bde358c08ba9849544a8382ff7abce32dbae1ade3f8676926cd8054cb9f152bf9c6f409aa16a6380b7eeecec5be805720d62587fdb21b4f4eceb7fc8ea03e6a6', 'eec15c47bdddaa6572a3eeb08cc53fb54e95faa33832e8776966e1cf9b54d1502e89defe6d249056c12cf75ccf4ff903988599aa790ef6505d98e05121a7cafa', '3a116268872fb075be056c9710abb11134514dab0ec7fe91a1df2280b5f755f344d6e7a62fa4d21ebccc54cf37a3545f8334785ec5baa6f9ccd2c75f8b350dd0', '9d9b00da6994ba8d7997d53ef20c54353fe531f514c3646c5194f5970af13da23a525d6478e2db0950e61e3e8afefadd5d1eb0f88358c4d18c37fcbd2916681c'], 'frequency': 6, 'degree': 8}, {'id': '7953e0f4-edb8-4148-bb10-a5a92cba553c', 'human_readable_id': 1, 'title': 'GEORGE GARR HENRY', 'type': 'PERSON', 'description': 'George Garr Henry is recognized as the author of the document titled "How to Invest Money." In addition to his work as an author, he held a significant position in the financial sector, serving as Vice-President of the Guaranty Trust Company, based in New York. His dual roles in literature and finance illustrate a deep understanding of investment and financial principles, likely influencing both his writing and his professional endeavors in the banking industry.', 'text_unit_ids': ['69b0e67c5fa9a5c565b1ea749505fd17c5c4af6ffd0316151c996811d2e0af417ae08600bea4659287b6631162541117c43dfe4a8e29abf6a9ff98e394a00e33', '4d53b154bd12c2d67fa71e4903629fce3f712b84bef668891feedc8e67e5dfed7165bd5f38fa34cca09426adfd5441fa45f95f26684e1bbd0666493af5dd0868'], 'frequency': 2, 'degree': 4}, {'id': 'b085bc27-cd68-410a-af7d-a10a8958dfec', 'human_readable_id': 2, 'title': 'THE INTERNET ARCHIVE/AMERICAN LIBRARIES', 'type': 'ORGANIZATION', 'description': 'The Internet Archive and American Libraries provided images that contributed to the production of this eBook by Julia Neufeld and the Online Distributed Proofreading Team.', 'text_unit_ids': ['69b0e67c5fa9a5c565b1ea749505fd17c5c4af6ffd0316151c996811d2e0af417ae08600bea4659287b6631162541117c43dfe4a8e29abf6a9ff98e394a00e33'], 'frequency': 1, 'degree': 2}, {'id': 'd6193f98-d219-46ef-ac61-e16dcd1a1332', 'human_readable_id': 3, 'title': 'FUNK & WAGNALLS COMPANY', 'type': 'ORGANIZATION', 'description': "Funk & Wagnalls Company is the publisher of 'How to Invest Money', based in New York and London.", 'text_unit_ids': ['69b0e67c5fa9a5c565b1ea749505fd17c5c4af6ffd0316151c996811d2e0af417ae08600bea4659287b6631162541117c43dfe4a8e29abf6a9ff98e394a00e33'], 'frequency': 1, 'degree': 2}, {'id': '7d305be4-3faa-417c-93a0-6831d698fc47', 'human_readable_id': 4, 'title': 'UNITED STATES', 'type': 'GEO', 'description': "The United States is a country characterized by significant industrial and legal frameworks, especially in relation to its railroads and literary contributions. Economically, the nation boasts an average total capitalization per mile for all railroads standing at $67,936, indicating the substantial investment and infrastructure present in its rail transportation sector.\n\nBeyond its economic activities, the United States holds a pivotal role in the literary and digital domain, specifically through its association with Project Gutenberg. This globally recognized project, which provides free access to a wide range of eBooks, operates primarily under the legal framework of the United States. This association with the U.S. significantly influences the project's copyright and donation policies, given that Project Gutenberg's legal infrastructure is designed in compliance with American laws.\n\nAdditionally, the Project Gutenberg Literary Archive Foundation, which is responsible for managing donations and maintaining the project’s operations, complies strictly with charitable laws within the United States. This compliance ensures that the Foundation can effectively manage its resources and continue to expand its accessible repository of literary works, supported by generous contributions from donors who are assured of the Foundation's legitimacy and lawful conduct in the United States.\n\nMoreover, the geographical significance of the United States in the context of Project Gutenberg extends further as the nation is mentioned within the framework of the project's jurisdiction for eBook use. This indicates the prominence and influence of U.S. law and policy in governing and facilitating the availability and distribution of digital literary content provided by Project Gutenberg.\n\nIn summary, the United States plays a critical role both as a geographical location and as the primary legal and economic framework for notable projects such as Project Gutenberg. The country’s strong railroad infrastructure and its adherence to a robust legal framework for digital content distribution underscore its status as a central hub for both industrial and intellectual development.", 'text_unit_ids': ['69b0e67c5fa9a5c565b1ea749505fd17c5c4af6ffd0316151c996811d2e0af417ae08600bea4659287b6631162541117c43dfe4a8e29abf6a9ff98e394a00e33', '7f483ec53b3fe675d6dbf3ee570720c4ee1fa1dbaaa1d05df8a268469e7b0567da4410c48ad05f2bc00ecb4b1a51bf26d66739196d68c6af47b3cbf08c54096b', '3a116268872fb075be056c9710abb11134514dab0ec7fe91a1df2280b5f755f344d6e7a62fa4d21ebccc54cf37a3545f8334785ec5baa6f9ccd2c75f8b350dd0', '9d9b00da6994ba8d7997d53ef20c54353fe531f514c3646c5194f5970af13da23a525d6478e2db0950e61e3e8afefadd5d1eb0f88358c4d18c37fcbd2916681c'], 'frequency': 4, 'degree': 5}], 'relationships': [{'id': 'bc49a0c2-204c-4511-b9fe-1833aaacb644', 'human_readable_id': 0, 'source': 'GEORGE GARR HENRY', 'target': 'GUARANTY TRUST COMPANY', 'description': 'George Garr Henry was Vice-President of the Guaranty Trust Company.', 'weight': 8.0,